# Receipt scanner configuration (optional)
#
# The app works fully without these values: manual entry never leaves the device.
# Scanning a receipt is the only feature that talks to the network.
#
# Option A — RECOMMENDED for any shared or production build
# Point the app at your own backend/serverless proxy so the Gemini API key
# stays on the server and is never embedded in the app bundle.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GEMINI_PROXY_URL=https://your-proxy.example.com/scan
#
# The proxy receives { base64Image, mimeType } as JSON and must return the
# receipt JSON documented in src/services/receiptScanner.ts.
#
# Option B — local / personal builds only
# Any EXPO_PUBLIC_* value is inlined into the JavaScript bundle and can be
# extracted from an installed app, so never ship a shared build with a key.
# Restrict the key in Google Cloud Console to the Generative Language API and
# to your Android package + SHA-1 (and iOS bundle id). There is no equivalent
# restriction for the web build.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GEMINI_API_KEY=
